Z||000000||Fiero*101||12-17-2001||07:39 PM||||THROTAL BODY is gunked up and ICS is stuck<BR>carb cleaner will help clean it out.<BR>if that does not work try pulling off the el plugs on the TB and spray them with WD-40 on both sides ck wires and allso ck grounds on motor to frame.<P>whats this mean? I know what the throttle body is but how do i do this procedure and what is the ICS? and the EL plugs<BR>thanks<BR><P>------------------<BR>Fiero*101<BR>Gold 86 SE 2M6<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mycar101.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||johnt671||12-17-2001||08:56 PM||||If you look on the tb on the left hand side you will see a set of three or four (I think) wires at the back of the tb.  These run to the IAC.  unplug the connector and you'll see the IAC I used an adjustable wrench to remove to .  the body of it has a large nut.  Just unscrew it and it will give you access to the inner part of the air passages and the business end of the IAC  Clean both parts with a spray cleaner and reassemble.  It about a ten min. job.  You will have to drive the car over 35 mph to reset the IAC and it may take a few days for the computer to adjust to the clean passages.<p>[This message has been edited by johnt671 (edited 12-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fiero*101||12-17-2001||11:15 PM||||Thanks for the info<P>ok now what is the ICS?<BR>sombody told me it might be stuck i cant remember which member told me that but what is it and how do i unstick it?<P>------------------<BR>Fiero*101<BR>Gold 86 SE 2M6<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mycar101.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||GTDude||12-18-2001||12:14 AM||||Well they should have said ISC instead of ICS which means "idle speed control" but is the incorrect term for this car.  You have an IAC which is an "idle air control".  That's the thing you need to clean and the passages. It's easy, but be sure to get a flashlight and make sure you get all the gunk off of where the little pintacle on the iac seats in the throttle body.  If not.....use a rag and screwdriver soaked in tb cleaner.  Hope this helps!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/DSCF0003a.JPG"> ||||reg||1
